{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788741116916276302,"compiled_state":{"alias":"smoggy-republican-saiga","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7d1d92b0ac67cbf4d820f7cc46c4aa31e37baa7d069e0974ccc91c9e6f2b52af","event_uuid":"3ac9466c-5b8d-43d3-8df7-add09f74ac49","position":{"commit_sha":"a3a55fd40e2096aa495b736ec92a3bde6974cbcf","position":"1788735407771398437-3ac9466c-5b8d-43d3-8df7-add09f74ac49"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d7214ec325dd7091faa4c433f0af199855fa60b35503440b3dea0aa5dae380bd","event_uuid":"32330452-03ad-4e1b-b9a9-68b86749900c","position":{"commit_sha":"729a0d3d9fd3c9b40abb6caa633ac871f99adfd6","position":"1788735416184907795-32330452-03ad-4e1b-b9a9-68b86749900c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"20487bd0cda596ffc81ce2daecddfcbfbd806d4daa04c169e6a828bf094ec5af","event_uuid":"03e61734-94c5-4c36-ac31-f781ad8231c1","position":{"commit_sha":"ddb636157a22a561df1bd49cc0be7e760c23d617","position":"1788737387721494001-03e61734-94c5-4c36-ac31-f781ad8231c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (complete; investigation only)\n\nOBSERVATION\nThe ticket reports that `attach_commits` successfully recorded merged SHA `ea394c34...` on `goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle`, but the close precheck still failed with “no commit references it.” Code inspection matches: attached commits are read by `_attached_commit_shas`, but not considered by the presence check that decides whether work “landed.”\n\nHYPOTHESIS\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_work_landed` computes `referencing = _referencing_commits(...)` and raises when `own_impact and not referencing`. The function calls `_check_file_impact_vs_diff(...)` only after that raise point. The attached-commit source is unioned later inside `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:_check_file_impact_vs_diff`, so attachments can validate diff impact but cannot satisfy the earlier “at least one landed commit exists” predicate.\n\nCONFIRMATION\nConfirmed with a deterministic monkeypatch experiment: `_union_file_impact` and `field_reads.file_impact` returned `['src/a.py']`, `_referencing_commits` returned `[]`, `_attached_commit_shas` returned `['attached-sha']`, and `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` was instrumented. `_check_work_landed(...)` raised the existing “no commit references it” error and the diff checker was never called (`DIFF_CALLS 0`). This would have been disproven if the attached SHA had been unioned into the presence decision or if the diff checker had run.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX DIRECTION\nMake `_check_work_landed` decide presence over the union of trailer-discovered commits and valid attached commits, while keeping the existing asymmetric unreadable-SHA policy and the later file-impact validation over both sources.","timestamp":1788737387721494001}],"created_at":1788735407771398437,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"32330452-03ad-4e1b-b9a9-68b86749900c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"36f4-ae53-2199-42c1"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`attach_commits` is documented as the repair path that lets the close gate tie a ticket to a landed change when no usable trailer can be discovered. During closure of `goldfilled-portly-dungbeetle`, attaching the valid merged SHA `ea394c34d13745cc0a14cea968b32f435ef15711` succeeded and the ticket state showed it under `commits`, but the deterministic close precheck still failed with “no commit references it.”\n\nThe implementation explains the contradiction: `_check_work_landed` rejects when `_referencing_commits(...)` is empty before `_attached_commit_shas(...)` is considered. Attached SHAs are used only by the later file-impact-vs-diff check.\n\n## Approach\nMake the work-landed presence decision use the union of trailer-discovered commits and validated ticket-attached commits, while retaining the existing path-impact validation and unreadable-commit policy. Add regression coverage through the close-precheck seam.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A file-impact ticket with a valid attached implementation commit passes the deterministic “work landed” presence check when no trailer-discovered commit is reachable from HEAD.\n- [ ] Attached and trailer-discovered commits are both checked against the declared file impact.\n- [ ] An absent attachment and absent trailer-discovered commit still fails closed with the existing actionable error.\n- [ ] An unreadable attached SHA retains the documented cross-clone behavior.\n- [ ] Tests cover the repaired close-precheck behavior without weakening normal trailer scanning.\n\n## Evidence\nObserved on ticket `36f4-ae53-2199-42c1`. Relevant seams: `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py::_check_work_landed`, `_attached_commit_shas`, and `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["bug","completion-gate","commit-traceability"],"ticket_id":"5623-98ad-dc87-49fa","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Close gate ignores attached commits for landing proof","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3ac9466c-5b8d-43d3-8df7-add09f74ac49","32330452-03ad-4e1b-b9a9-68b86749900c","03e61734-94c5-4c36-ac31-f781ad8231c1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788741116916276302,"uuid":"59db7953-3582-4932-adaa-dcbce2f1378b"}